$ cessna210_flagship_mloads.bdf — SOL 144 transient maneuver driver (Step 65)
$
$ Phase G0, DLM-free: a Level-1 quasi-steady, open-loop, restrained-l-set
$ Newmark-beta time integration seeded from the static 1g cruise trim.
$
$   SUBCASE 1  TRIM 1     the static 1g cruise trim (the MLOADS initial
$                         condition, solved and reported in its own right)
$   SUBCASE 2  MLOADS 1   elevator ramp: +2 deg over 0.3 s from the trimmed
$                         angle, then held to 1.0 s
$
$ Outputs: .f06 (trim block for SUBCASE 1 + transient maneuver block for
$ SUBCASE 2), <stem>.mldprnt.txt ASCII time history, and
$ <stem>.maneuver_qs_loads.bdf FORCE/MOMENT cards for the critical sample.
$
$ TWO-PASS AUTHORING.  MLDCOMD tables are ABSOLUTE, so TABLED1 300 in the bulk
$ file starts at the trimmed elevator angle (-0.065992 rad).  If the airframe,
$ the mass set or the flight condition changes, re-run
$ cessna210_flagship_trim.bdf and rewrite that first table point.
$
$ What to look for: at t = 0 every recovered quantity must equal the SUBCASE 1
$ trim exactly (the IC is that trim), and once the command has been held long
$ enough the response settles toward the static trim of the same airplane with
$ ELEV prescribed at the held value.  Both are gated by the test suite.
$
$ Walk-through: docs/20_theory/02_realistic_airplane_sol144.md
$ Units: SI (m, N, kg, Pa, s)
$
SOL 144
TITLE = Cessna 210 flagship — elevator-ramp pull-up (MLOADS)
INCLUDE 'cessna210_flagship_bulk.bdf'
$
SUBCASE 1
  TITLE = 1g cruise trim (MLOADS initial condition)
  TRIM  = 1
  SPC   = 1
$
SUBCASE 2
  TITLE  = Elevator ramp +2 deg over 0.3 s, held
  MLOADS = 1
  SPC    = 1
$
BEGIN BULK
ENDDATA
